WEBVTT

00:00:03.581 --> 00:00:08.122
Chida presents Halloween Horror by Gina D.B.

00:00:08.182 --> 00:00:19.878
Clement.

00:00:19.938 --> 00:00:36.076
Naum Keog, City of Peace, is its Indian name.

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:43.392
But it is also called the Witch City, because of the witch hangings of 1692.

00:00:43.452 --> 00:00:47.876
There are seven historical witch museums in Salem.

00:00:47.936 --> 00:00:54.980
They all have a lot of information on the witches and hangings of 1692.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:59.850
Kelly and Megan Conner are two sisters.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:03.356
They come from San Francisco, California.

00:01:03.416 --> 00:01:11.380
The Connor family now lives in Salem because Mr. Connor teaches French at the University of Boston.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:15.732
Kelly is 14 and Meghan is 13.

00:01:15.792 --> 00:01:19.984
They go to Salem Middle School and they like it.

00:01:20.044 --> 00:01:23.006
Kelly has red hair and blue eyes.

00:01:23.066 --> 00:01:26.972
She's tall and plays basketball for the school team.

00:01:27.032 --> 00:01:30.508
Megan has fair hair and blue eyes.

00:01:30.568 --> 00:01:32.761
She's a champion swimmer.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.234
She is a member of the Salem Swimming Team.

00:01:36.294 --> 00:01:39.208
It's Friday, October 28th.

00:01:39.268 --> 00:01:43.161
And Halloween is on Monday, October 31st.

00:01:43.221 --> 00:01:48.086
Kelly and Megan are very excited because they love Halloween.

00:01:48.146 --> 00:01:52.758
This is their first Halloween in Salem, the Witch City.

00:01:52.818 --> 00:01:55.378
I think about Halloween all the time.

00:01:55.438 --> 00:01:56.448
Says Megan.

00:01:56.508 --> 00:01:57.488
Me too.

00:01:57.548 --> 00:01:59.369
Says Kelly.

00:01:59.429 --> 00:02:03.100
We must buy a pumpkin and make a jack-o'-lantern.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:04.140
Says their mother.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.731
Now finish your breakfast.

00:02:05.791 --> 00:02:06.471
It's late.

00:02:06.531 --> 00:02:09.872
School starts in 20 minutes.

00:02:09.932 --> 00:02:14.693
The girls eat their eggs and drink their milk.

00:02:14.753 --> 00:02:17.774
Then they go upstairs to brush their teeth.

00:02:17.834 --> 00:02:20.870
They're ready at quarter past eight.

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:22.336
Goodbye, Mom!

00:02:22.396 --> 00:02:24.668
Don't forget to buy the pumpkin!

00:02:24.728 --> 00:02:28.129
Okay, goodbye, girls!

00:02:28.189 --> 00:02:32.402
Kelly and Meghan always walk to school.

00:02:32.462 --> 00:02:39.146
They meet their friends, Susan Garcia, Nick Lee, and Bill Goldberg.

00:02:39.206 --> 00:02:43.649
I'm so excited about Halloween, says Susan.

00:02:43.709 --> 00:02:46.041
Susan is Hispanic American.

00:02:46.101 --> 00:02:49.683
She is 13 years old and has long black hair.

00:02:49.743 --> 00:02:53.745
This is the first time we can have a party without our parents.

00:02:53.805 --> 00:02:57.416
We must find a place to have the party.

00:02:57.476 --> 00:03:03.079
Says Nick, he is 14 years old and he's a good cook.

00:03:03.139 --> 00:03:06.071
His parents have a Chinese restaurant in Salem.

00:03:06.131 --> 00:03:07.101
Let's see.

00:03:07.161 --> 00:03:10.343
Says Bill, I can ask my grandmother.

00:03:10.403 --> 00:03:13.805
Bill Goldberg is a handsome boy of 14.

00:03:13.864 --> 00:03:16.976
His favorite school subject is science.

00:03:17.036 --> 00:03:19.261
He lives with his grandmother.

00:03:19.321 --> 00:03:22.912
Susan, do you have a scary costume for Halloween?

00:03:22.972 --> 00:03:24.115
Asks Kelly.

00:03:24.175 --> 00:03:26.466
It's a surprise, I can't tell you.

00:03:26.526 --> 00:03:27.552
says Susan.

00:03:27.612 --> 00:03:29.483
Do you believe in ghosts?

00:03:29.543 --> 00:03:30.734
Bill asks.

00:03:30.794 --> 00:03:31.914
Yes.

00:03:31.974 --> 00:03:33.005
They all say.

00:03:33.065 --> 00:03:34.486
Oh, I don't.

00:03:34.546 --> 00:03:35.416
Says Bill.

00:03:35.476 --> 00:03:38.057
Science can explain everything.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:38.888
Really?

00:03:38.948 --> 00:03:39.958
Says Nick.

00:03:40.018 --> 00:03:43.260
A lot of strange things happen on Halloween night.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.411
My grandparents come from China.

00:03:45.471 --> 00:03:48.752
They believe in ghosts and evil spirits too.

00:03:48.812 --> 00:03:50.361
Bill laughs.

00:03:50.421 --> 00:03:55.072
Do you remember the story of the old woman in the cemetery?

00:03:55.132 --> 00:03:59.525
Oh, Nick, please don't tell us again, says Bill.

00:03:59.584 --> 00:04:02.126
Nick smiles mysteriously.

00:04:02.186 --> 00:04:04.058
It's 8.30 a.m.

00:04:04.118 --> 00:04:11.462
and the school bell is ringing.

00:04:11.522 --> 00:04:18.287
Chapter 2.

00:04:18.347 --> 00:04:23.115
The Witch Museum.

00:04:23.175 --> 00:04:29.064
School finishes at 3.30pm.

00:04:29.124 --> 00:04:32.686
Kelly and Meghan meet their friends outside.

00:04:32.746 --> 00:04:35.957
Do you have any ideas for our Halloween party?

00:04:36.017 --> 00:04:37.178
Kelly asks.

00:04:37.238 --> 00:04:38.538
No, I don't.

00:04:38.598 --> 00:04:39.609
Says Susan.

00:04:39.669 --> 00:04:40.930
I have an idea.

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:41.780
Says Meghan.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:44.492
Let's visit one of the Salem Witch Museums.

00:04:44.552 --> 00:04:47.524
We can get many ideas from there.

00:04:47.583 --> 00:04:49.584
That's a good idea.

00:04:49.644 --> 00:04:50.600
Says Susan.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:53.336
There are a lot of scary things there.

00:04:53.396 --> 00:04:57.146
Remember, Salem is the witch city.

00:04:57.206 --> 00:05:00.737
At the museum, there are pictures of the witch hangings.

00:05:00.797 --> 00:05:05.438
There are also the names of the Salem witches of 1692.

00:05:05.498 --> 00:05:09.050
We can read about their terrible magic.

00:05:09.109 --> 00:05:11.490
Oh, how exciting!

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:12.980
Say Megan and Kelly.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:14.041
Let's go.

00:05:14.061 --> 00:05:15.236
Says Susan.

00:05:15.296 --> 00:05:18.143
The girls call Nick and Bill.

00:05:18.203 --> 00:05:21.406
Together the five friends go to the museum.

00:05:21.465 --> 00:05:24.248
When they arrive, it's late.

00:05:24.308 --> 00:05:26.169
How many tickets do you want?

00:05:26.229 --> 00:05:27.641
Asks the attendant.

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:30.343
Five tickets please, says Bill.

00:05:30.402 --> 00:05:31.994
That's ten dollars.

00:05:32.054 --> 00:05:35.266
Remember the museum closes at five p.m.

00:05:35.326 --> 00:05:37.438
You only have half an hour.

00:05:37.498 --> 00:05:40.631
The five friends walk around the museum.

00:05:40.691 --> 00:05:43.350
They look at the interesting exhibits.

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:48.302
Look, here are the names of the witches of 1692.

00:05:48.362 --> 00:05:50.906
And here are the pictures of the hangings.

00:05:50.965 --> 00:05:51.896
Says Nick.

00:05:51.956 --> 00:05:53.408
Look at this rope.

00:05:53.468 --> 00:05:54.480
Says Bill.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:56.572
How scary!

00:05:56.632 --> 00:05:57.723
Say the girls.

00:05:57.783 --> 00:05:59.165
I'm going upstairs.

00:05:59.224 --> 00:05:59.865
Says Megan.

00:05:59.925 --> 00:06:00.796
Be careful.

00:06:00.856 --> 00:06:01.798
Says Kelly.

00:06:01.858 --> 00:06:03.379
Megan laugh.

00:06:03.438 --> 00:06:09.333
I'm not afraid of witches or ghosts.

00:06:09.393 --> 00:06:14.806
There are no visitors upstairs.

00:06:14.866 --> 00:06:18.718
There is a sweet smell of roses in the air.

00:06:18.778 --> 00:06:22.291
Meghan walks around and looks at everything.

00:06:22.351 --> 00:06:25.494
Then she sees an old lady.

00:06:25.554 --> 00:06:30.257
She has a long black dress with small black buttons.

00:06:30.317 --> 00:06:35.150
Her skin is very white and her lips are very red.

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:39.254
There is a strange red mark around her neck.

00:06:39.314 --> 00:06:41.685
She smiles at Meghan.

00:06:41.745 --> 00:06:45.857
Megan smiles too, but she is nerfs.

00:06:45.917 --> 00:06:49.569
Suddenly the air is very cold.

00:06:49.629 --> 00:06:51.440
How strange!

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:52.330
She thinks.

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:59.004
I want to go downstairs.

00:06:59.064 --> 00:07:06.053
When Kelly sees her, she asks.

00:07:06.113 --> 00:07:07.649
What's upstairs?

00:07:07.709 --> 00:07:09.810
Oh, some interesting exhibits.

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:11.181
Answers, Meghan.

00:07:11.241 --> 00:07:14.372
The museum closes in five minutes.

00:07:14.432 --> 00:07:16.374
Says the attendant.

00:07:16.434 --> 00:07:21.987
Susan buys a book called Salem and the Witches of 1692.

00:07:22.027 --> 00:07:26.690
The three girls walk to the front door.

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:29.621
Is there anyone still upstairs?

00:07:29.681 --> 00:07:31.062
Ask the attendant.

00:07:31.122 --> 00:07:32.012
Yes.

00:07:32.072 --> 00:07:32.983
Says Meghan.

00:07:33.043 --> 00:07:34.629
There's an old lady.

00:07:34.689 --> 00:07:35.654
Really?

00:07:35.714 --> 00:07:36.916
Says the attendant.

00:07:36.976 --> 00:07:38.377
That's strange.

00:07:38.437 --> 00:07:42.100
You are the only visitors in the museum this afternoon.

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:45.102
There aren't many visitors here on Fridays.

00:07:45.162 --> 00:07:47.424
There is an old lady upstairs.

00:07:47.484 --> 00:07:48.726
Says Megan.

00:07:48.785 --> 00:07:51.258
I'm going upstairs to see.

00:07:51.318 --> 00:07:53.100
Says the attendant.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.889
After a few minutes, he returns.

00:07:55.949 --> 00:08:00.480
His face is red, and he says, Is this a joke?

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:06.856
There's no one upstairs, and the only door of the museum is this front door.

00:08:06.916 --> 00:08:09.458
Meghan's friends look at her.

00:08:09.518 --> 00:08:11.150
She is silent.

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:14.502
Then she says, Let's look outside.

00:08:14.562 --> 00:08:18.285
They run out of the museum and look outside.

00:08:18.345 --> 00:08:20.777
There's no one in the street.

00:08:20.837 --> 00:08:23.716
Only a black cat.

00:08:23.776 --> 00:08:29.254
After this strange experience, they walk home.

00:08:29.314 --> 00:08:34.567
Now I have a lot of ideas for a Halloween party.

00:08:34.627 --> 00:08:35.667
Says Kelly.

00:08:35.727 --> 00:08:37.248
Yes, I do too.

00:08:37.308 --> 00:08:38.338
Says Susan.

00:08:38.398 --> 00:08:40.289
You're very quiet, Megan.

00:08:40.349 --> 00:08:41.240
Says Bill.

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:49.714
I'm thinking about the old lady at the museum.

00:08:49.774 --> 00:08:56.538
Hello.

00:08:56.598 --> 00:08:58.678
Is the museum still open?

00:08:58.738 --> 00:09:00.309
Yes, it is.

00:09:00.369 --> 00:09:02.650
Five tickets, please.

00:09:02.710 --> 00:09:04.160
Are you students?

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:05.851
Yes, we are.

00:09:05.911 --> 00:09:08.132
Then you have a special price.

00:09:08.192 --> 00:09:10.633
It's ten dollars for each student.

00:09:10.693 --> 00:09:12.144
Here you are.

00:09:12.204 --> 00:09:15.455
Do you have any information about the museum?

00:09:15.515 --> 00:09:16.505
Yes.

00:09:16.565 --> 00:09:19.616
There are some books near the window over there.

00:09:19.676 --> 00:09:22.147
What time does the museum close?

00:09:22.207 --> 00:09:27.127
It closes at five.

00:09:27.188 --> 00:09:38.731
The origins of Halloween, date, 22 AD, place, British Isles.

00:09:38.791 --> 00:09:42.123
Hello, my name is Brennis.

00:09:42.182 --> 00:09:44.784
I'm a Salt and a Pagan.

00:09:44.844 --> 00:09:49.236
Let me tell you about an important Celtic festival.

00:09:49.296 --> 00:09:57.132
Samhain is the last day of summer and the last day of the Celtic year, October 31st.

00:09:57.192 --> 00:10:01.124
Samhain is the Celtic god of death.

00:10:01.184 --> 00:10:03.634
We are all afraid of him.

00:10:03.694 --> 00:10:09.786
On October 31st, we dress as witches, ghosts, and skeletons.

00:10:09.846 --> 00:10:13.328
We make fires to scare the evil spirits.

00:10:13.388 --> 00:10:17.558
We also play games to bring good luck in the new year.

00:10:17.618 --> 00:10:18.709
Oh!

00:10:18.769 --> 00:10:25.441
And the apples we eat are for good luck, too.

00:10:25.501 --> 00:10:39.328
Chapter 3 September 22, 1692 There is no school on Saturday.

00:10:39.388 --> 00:10:42.379
It is a cloudy autumn day.

00:10:42.439 --> 00:10:46.661
Autumn is usually a beautiful season in Salem.

00:10:46.721 --> 00:10:51.394
The leaves on the trees are yellow, red, and orange.

00:10:51.454 --> 00:10:56.920
Mr. and Mrs. Connor have a big orange pumpkin.

00:10:56.980 --> 00:10:59.676
They are making a jack-o'-lantern.

00:10:59.736 --> 00:11:05.190
When it's finished, we can put it in front of the window, says Mr. Connor.

00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:08.022
Are you girls ready for Halloween?

00:11:08.082 --> 00:11:09.143
No, Dad.

00:11:09.203 --> 00:11:11.295
We must find a place for the party.

00:11:11.355 --> 00:11:12.336
Says Kelly.

00:11:12.396 --> 00:11:14.558
We must make our costumes, too.

00:11:14.618 --> 00:11:15.688
Says Megan.

00:11:15.748 --> 00:11:18.951
Today is a perfect day to do many things.

00:11:19.011 --> 00:11:20.291
Says Mrs. Connor.

00:11:20.351 --> 00:11:22.381
Finish your homework this morning.

00:11:22.441 --> 00:11:25.982
Then you can look for a place for the party this afternoon.

00:11:26.042 --> 00:11:28.223
I can start my science homework.

00:11:28.283 --> 00:11:29.313
Says Megan.

00:11:29.373 --> 00:11:31.294
I'm a study English.

00:11:31.354 --> 00:11:32.524
Says Kelly.

00:11:32.584 --> 00:11:34.835
I have a test on Wednesday.

00:11:34.895 --> 00:11:38.616
They go to their room and study until noon.

00:11:38.676 --> 00:11:43.554
Then the phone rings.

00:11:43.614 --> 00:11:48.933
Hello, this is Bill.

00:11:48.993 --> 00:11:50.994
I have a place for our party.

00:11:51.054 --> 00:11:51.774
Really?

00:11:51.834 --> 00:11:53.696
That's great, where is it?

00:11:53.756 --> 00:11:54.716
Says Kelly.

00:11:54.776 --> 00:11:56.297
It's a surprise.

00:11:56.357 --> 00:11:59.969
Meet me and Nick in front of the school at 1.30pm.

00:12:00.028 --> 00:12:01.520
We can go together.

00:12:01.579 --> 00:12:03.851
Okay, at half past one then.

00:12:03.911 --> 00:12:06.302
Says Kelly.

00:12:06.362 --> 00:12:10.744
The five friends meet in front of their school.

00:12:10.804 --> 00:12:12.724
They are very excited.

00:12:12.784 --> 00:12:14.204
Where is the place?

00:12:14.264 --> 00:12:15.334
Ask Susan.

00:12:15.394 --> 00:12:17.086
Follow me, says Bill.

00:12:17.146 --> 00:12:19.317
My grandmother knows this place.

00:12:19.377 --> 00:12:22.969
It is the best place for a spooky Halloween party.

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:28.322
They walk past the park, past the tennis courts, and past the church.

00:12:28.382 --> 00:12:30.974
Then they walk down a country road.

00:12:31.034 --> 00:12:35.156
At the end of the road, they see an old cemetery.

00:12:35.216 --> 00:12:39.410
This is the oldest cemetery in Salem, says Bill.

00:12:39.470 --> 00:12:42.173
They enter the old cemetery.

00:12:42.233 --> 00:12:44.726
Look at the dates on the tombstones.

00:12:44.786 --> 00:12:46.637
This one says September 22, 1692.

00:12:46.657 --> 00:12:47.257
Says Meghan.

00:12:47.277 --> 00:12:48.658
This one says September 22, 1692.

00:12:48.698 --> 00:12:49.158
Says Kelly.

00:12:49.178 --> 00:12:51.399
Here's another tombstone with the same date.

00:12:51.459 --> 00:12:52.259
September 22, 1692.

00:12:52.299 --> 00:12:58.339
Says Nick.

00:12:58.399 --> 00:13:06.321
They look at a lot of tombstones.

00:13:06.381 --> 00:13:09.904
These are probably the tombstones of the Salem Witches.

00:13:09.964 --> 00:13:10.944
Says Bill.

00:13:11.004 --> 00:13:12.365
How spooky!

00:13:12.425 --> 00:13:13.676
Let's go now!

00:13:13.736 --> 00:13:15.308
Says Susan.

00:13:15.368 --> 00:13:18.940
The five friends run to the country road.

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:21.572
Then they walk for a few minutes.

00:13:21.632 --> 00:13:26.116
At the end of the road they see an old abandoned house.

00:13:26.176 --> 00:13:28.448
It is near a forest.

00:13:28.508 --> 00:13:31.724
There is a rose bush near the door.

00:13:31.784 --> 00:13:35.550
This is the house for our party, says Bill.

00:13:35.610 --> 00:13:38.351
His friends are very surprised.

00:13:38.411 --> 00:13:40.202
They look at the house.

00:13:40.262 --> 00:13:41.513
Wow!

00:13:41.573 --> 00:13:43.284
Is this a haunted house?

00:13:43.344 --> 00:13:44.555
Nick asks.

00:13:44.614 --> 00:13:46.636
Bill laughs.

00:13:46.695 --> 00:13:51.188
This is a very old house from the 1650s.

00:13:51.248 --> 00:13:55.400
Poor people sometimes live in it, but then they go away.

00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:56.811
It's abandoned.

00:13:56.871 --> 00:13:58.832
There is no electricity.

00:13:58.892 --> 00:14:00.903
Why is it abandoned?

00:14:00.963 --> 00:14:02.263
Asks Nick.

00:14:02.323 --> 00:14:05.464
They say strange things happen here.

00:14:05.524 --> 00:14:08.966
It's the perfect place for a spooky party.

00:14:09.026 --> 00:14:12.468
Remember, ghosts don't exist.

00:14:12.528 --> 00:14:13.488
Bill says.

00:14:13.548 --> 00:14:14.990
Are you sure?

00:14:15.050 --> 00:14:16.510
Asks Kelly.

00:14:16.570 --> 00:14:19.352
The five friends look at each other.

00:14:19.412 --> 00:14:22.504
There is something strange about this place.

00:14:22.564 --> 00:14:26.576
Says Nick.

00:14:26.636 --> 00:14:36.946
Chapter 4 the abandoned house.

00:14:37.006 --> 00:14:46.898
Megan looks at the old house and says, Look at the writing above the door.

00:14:46.958 --> 00:14:53.589
Home of Abigail Cross October 31, 1627 to September 22, 1692.

00:14:53.609 --> 00:14:58.697
Who is Abigail Cross?

00:14:58.757 --> 00:15:07.098
Look at the date, September 22, 1692.

00:15:07.158 --> 00:15:09.880
Do you remember the tombstones?

00:15:09.940 --> 00:15:13.414
Many of them have the same date.

00:15:13.474 --> 00:15:16.206
You're right, says Susan.

00:15:16.266 --> 00:15:21.770
Let me look in my new book, Salem and the Witches of 1692.

00:15:21.829 --> 00:15:26.818
After a few minutes, Susan says, Oh no!

00:15:26.878 --> 00:15:29.769
Abigail Cross is a witch.

00:15:29.829 --> 00:15:32.340
Her name is in this book.

00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:34.962
I don't like this old house.

00:15:35.022 --> 00:15:37.573
Let's find another place for the party.

00:15:37.633 --> 00:15:38.873
Says Kelly.

00:15:38.933 --> 00:15:40.794
You girls are silly.

00:15:40.854 --> 00:15:42.015
This is perfect.

00:15:42.075 --> 00:15:42.875
Says Bill.

00:15:42.935 --> 00:15:46.237
Come on, follow me.

00:15:46.297 --> 00:15:50.809
Bill is the first to enter the house.

00:15:50.869 --> 00:15:53.323
Nick and the girls follow.

