00:43:15.170 --> 00:43:19.738
Make a bat.

00:43:19.798 --> 00:43:27.872
You need a square piece of paper colored on one side and white on the other side.

00:43:27.932 --> 00:43:30.534
A pair of scissors.

00:43:30.594 --> 00:43:32.434
1.

00:43:32.495 --> 00:43:38.007
Fold the square in half from top to bottom.

00:43:38.027 --> 00:43:38.457
2.

00:43:38.517 --> 00:43:43.386
Fold and unfold in half from side to side.

00:43:43.446 --> 00:43:48.924
Three, fold one half up along the middle fold line.

00:43:48.984 --> 00:43:52.135
Start to open out the paper.

00:43:52.195 --> 00:43:58.196
Four, and with your free hand, press it down.

00:43:58.256 --> 00:44:04.198
Five, neatly into a triangle.

00:44:04.259 --> 00:44:11.768
Six, turn the paper over, repeat steps two to five.

00:44:11.828 --> 00:44:13.665
7.

00:44:13.725 --> 00:44:17.856
Fold one of the right hand corners to the middle fold line.

00:44:17.916 --> 00:44:21.786
Do the same with the other left hand corner.

00:44:21.846 --> 00:44:23.527
8.

00:44:23.587 --> 00:44:29.798
Fold the right bottom corners in to make the bat's feet.

00:44:29.858 --> 00:44:31.888
9.

00:44:31.948 --> 00:44:34.989
Carefully cut the paper as shown.

00:44:35.049 --> 00:44:42.004
Fold the top point down, so making the bat's head and ears appear.

00:44:42.064 --> 00:44:43.617
10.

00:44:43.677 --> 00:44:49.150
To complete the bat, fold the tips of its feet out towards you.

00:44:49.210 --> 00:44:54.787
Don't forget to draw the eyes and fangs!

00:44:54.847 --> 00:44:56.882
.

00:44:56.942 --> 00:44:57.222
.

